    "description": "A logistics marketplace prices shipments differently per tenant: some tenants price per kilometre, others by weight brackets, a few by full cost-plus contracts, and two enterprise tenants need a rules engine driven by their own tariff file. The pricing service today is one 600-line method with a switch over the tenant type, plus quarterly patches that keep breaking the other branches. Marketing wants to add a promotional pricing scheme next quarter without touching the existing branches, and support wants to see which algorithm produced an offer. The decision to implement: how to encapsulate each pricing computation behind one common call so the caller picks one at runtime, new schemes can be added without editing existing branches, and each scheme stays independently testable.",
    "decision_statement": "Encapsulate each interchangeable pricing computation behind one common operation that the caller selects at runtime.",
    "notes": "template-method stays acceptable because the reviewer may prefer an inheritance-based variation."
